      en: "The Gounghin Royal Quarter in Ouagadougou, Burkina Faso, is the historic center of the Mossi kings. It houses the palace of the Mogho Naaba, the traditional ruler of the Mossi. The quarter features traditional mud-brick architecture and courtyards. Important cultural ceremonies take place here. Gounghin is a living testament to Mossi history. The palace complex includes multiple buildings, such as the audience hall and living quarters. The quarter is open to visitors, offering insights into royal tradition.",
